<div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto">
  <h1>Mentorship Programme</h1>
  <p style="font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--muted)">
    Connecting experienced alumni with students and early-career members.
  </p>

  <div class="stack-lg" style="margin-top: var(--space-6)">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>How It Works</h2>
      <ol style="line-height: var(--leading-loose)">
        <li>
          <strong>Find a mentor.</strong> Browse the
          <a href="/directory?mentor=1">directory</a> to see members who have
          opted into mentorship. Filter by industry or expertise.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Send a request.</strong> Click "Request mentorship" on their
          profile. Describe your goals and what you're looking for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>They respond.</strong> Your mentor can accept or decline
          within a few days. If they accept, you can arrange to meet.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Agree on goals.</strong> Discuss what you want to achieve.
          Mentors typically commit to 1–2 conversations per month for 3–6
          months.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Become a Mentor</h2>
      <p>
        If you have at least 2 years of professional experience and want to give
        back, you can opt in as a mentor in your
        <a href="/dashboard/profile">Profile Settings</a>. Toggle on "Available
        for mentorship" and specify your field of expertise.
      </p>
      <p>
        You control your availability. You can pause or pause mentorship at any
        time. All requests are visible to you first — you choose which to
        accept.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Guidelines</h2>
      <ul style="line-height: var(--leading-loose)">
        <li>
          Mentorship is voluntary and should be respectful, professional, and
          free of financial requests.
        </li>
        <li>
          All communication should be through HOSA's platform or agreed-upon
          channels.
        </li>
        <li>Both mentors and mentees can end the relationship at any time.</li>
        <li>
          For concerns or abuse reports, contact
          <a href="mailto:support@hosa-uganda.org">support@hosa-uganda.org</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: var(--space-6)">
      <a href="/register" class="btn btn--accent">Join HOSA to get started</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
